<section id="s1"><h2>1. Controller</h2>
<p>The controller within the meaning of the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and other applicable data-protection provisions is:</p>
<div class="box"><p><strong>Patrick Baust</strong><br>PaBaApps<br>Email: <a href="mailto:pabaapps@web.de">pabaapps@web.de</a></p></div></section>

<section id="s2"><h2>2. Scope</h2>
<p>This Privacy Policy explains the nature, scope and purposes of the processing of personal data when using the mobile application <strong>JobStamp</strong>.</p>
<p>It applies to all functions of the Android app and its related online services, in particular registration and sign-in, use of cloud functions, synchronisation between multiple devices, collaboration within a company, conclusion and management of paid subscriptions, support requests and all other app functions.</p>
<p>It applies regardless of whether JobStamp is used exclusively locally or additionally with cloud synchronisation.</p></section>

<section id="s3"><h2>3. Definitions</h2>
<p>This Privacy Policy uses the definitions of the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).</p>
<h3>Personal data</h3><p>Personal data means any information relating to an identified or identifiable natural person. This includes, for example, name, email address, telephone number or location data.</p>
<h3>Processing</h3><p>Processing means any operation performed on personal data, including in particular collection, storage, alteration, transmission, deletion or making data available.</p>
<h3>Controller</h3><p>The controller is the natural or legal person who determines the purposes and means of processing personal data.</p>
<h3>Processor</h3><p>A processor is a service provider that processes personal data solely on behalf of the controller.</p>
<h3>Company</h3><p>Within JobStamp, “company” means the organisation to which users, customers, jobs and other company data are assigned.</p></section>

<section id="s4"><h2>4. Principles of data processing</h2>
<p>The protection of personal data is very important to us. We process personal data only in accordance with the GDPR, applicable national data-protection laws and only to the extent necessary to provide the offered functions.</p>
<ul><li><strong>Data minimisation:</strong> Only personal data required for the respective function is processed.</li>
<li><strong>Purpose limitation:</strong> Personal data is processed only for the purposes described in this Privacy Policy.</li>
<li><strong>Storage limitation:</strong> Personal data is not stored longer than necessary or legally required.</li>
<li><strong>Integrity and confidentiality:</strong> Appropriate technical and organisational measures are used to protect personal data against loss, misuse or unauthorised access.</li></ul></section>

<section id="s5"><h2>5. Legal bases for processing</h2>
<p>Personal data is processed solely on the basis of the applicable legal bases under the GDPR. Depending on the processing activity, these may include:</p>
<ul><li><strong>Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR:</strong> processing based on freely given consent, for example when using location services or the camera.</li>
<li><strong>Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR:</strong> processing necessary for the performance of a contract or pre-contractual measures, for example to provide a user account or paid subscription.</li>
<li><strong>Art. 6(1)(c) GDPR:</strong> processing necessary to comply with a legal obligation.</li>
<li><strong>Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR:</strong> processing based on legitimate interests, in particular secure app operation, error analysis, system security and improvements to stability and usability.</li></ul></section>

<section id="s6"><h2>6. Registration and user account</h2>
<p>A user account is required to use JobStamp cloud functions. During registration, data may include in particular email address, username, authentication information, a unique user identifier and timestamps relating to registration and the most recent sign-in.</p>
<p>The processing serves in particular to identify users, assign company data, provide access to cloud functions, synchronise data and protect against unauthorised access. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR.</p></section>

<section id="s7"><h2>7. Sign-in with Google</h2>
<p>Users may alternatively sign in with an existing Google account. We receive only the information that Google provides as part of the authentication process, in particular name, email address and a unique Google user identifier.</p>
<p>The password of the Google account is never transmitted to or stored by us. Authentication is performed using Google's security mechanisms. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR.</p></section>

<section id="s8"><h2>8. Sign-in by email</h2>
<p>Alternatively, a user account can be created with an email address and a self-selected password. The password is not stored in plain text. Authentication is performed securely through our cloud infrastructure and is used solely to provide user-account management.</p></section>

<section id="s9"><h2>9. Local data storage (offline operation)</h2>
<p>JobStamp was developed according to an “offline first” principle. Core functions can be used without an active internet connection. Certain data is therefore stored locally on the device.</p>
<p>Depending on use, this may include user settings, company data, customers, jobs, categories, work-time entries, material catalogue, material usage, team members, calendar entries and temporary synchronisation information.</p>
<p>Local storage is used in particular for offline use, shorter loading times, prevention of data loss during connectivity interruptions and temporary storage until the next synchronisation. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR.</p></section>

<section id="s10"><h2>10. Cloud synchronisation</h2>
<p>JobStamp provides cloud synchronisation so that company data can be available on multiple devices and several authorised users can work together.</p>
<p>Data transmitted may include company data, customers, contact persons, jobs, work times, material data, categories, team members, settings and required synchronisation information.</p>
<p>Synchronisation is performed over an encrypted connection. Only data belonging to the company to which the respective user is assigned is synchronised. Data is not synchronised with unrelated companies. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR.</p></section>

<section id="s11"><h2>11. Company management</h2>
<p>Each user account can be assigned to a company or create a new company. Within a company, only data required to organise operational workflows is processed.</p>
<p>This may include company name, company address, telephone number, email address, optional company logo, internal settings, working-time configurations, categories and team members.</p></section>

<section id="s12"><h2>12. Roles and permissions</h2>
<p>JobStamp uses a role-based permission system to protect personal data. Different functions are available depending on the assigned role.</p>
<p>Roles can include, among others, owner, administrator, master/crafts supervisor, office staff, employee and apprentice. Depending on the role, users may for example manage customers, edit jobs, manage materials, track work times, manage team members or change company settings.</p></section>

<section id="s13"><h2>13. Team management</h2>
<p>Several users can work together within a company on shared company data. For team members, data may include in particular name, role, profession/trade and optionally email address and telephone number.</p>
<p>This data is used solely for collaboration within the relevant company. It is not disclosed to unrelated companies.</p></section>

<section id="s14"><h2>14. Customer management</h2>
<p>JobStamp allows customers and contact persons to be managed. Depending on use, this may include company name, contact person, address, telephone number, email address, notes, internal information and location information.</p>
<p>This data is used exclusively for planning, performing and documenting customer jobs.</p></section>

<section id="s15"><h2>15. Job management</h2>
<p>Jobs can be created and managed for customers. Data may include in particular job title, customer, category, status, planned execution date, assigned employees, material usage, work times and internal notes.</p></section>

<section id="s16"><h2>16. Time tracking</h2>
<p>JobStamp allows different time types to be recorded digitally, including work time, travel time, setup time and break time. Time entries may include start, end, duration, employee, customer, job and notes.</p>
<p>The data is used for documenting operational activities and internal evaluation. No automatic transmission to public authorities or social-security institutions takes place.</p></section>

<section id="s17"><h2>17. Calendar functions</h2>
<p>Work times and jobs can be displayed in different calendar views. Only existing company data is used for this purpose. JobStamp currently does not connect to external calendar services such as Google Calendar or Microsoft Outlook.</p></section>

<section id="s18"><h2>18. Material management</h2>
<p>JobStamp includes a material catalogue and material-usage management. Data may include in particular material name, category, internal article number, manufacturer article number, wholesaler article number, unit, package content, stock, usage and internal notes.</p>
<p>Price or purchasing information is processed only if it is entered by the company itself.</p></section>

<section id="s19"><h2>19. Camera and photos</h2>
<p>JobStamp allows users to take photos for documentation of customers, jobs or materials or to select existing images from the device.</p>
<p>Access to the camera or photo storage occurs only after prior consent through the operating-system permission system. Use is optional.</p>
<p>Photos can be used, for example, to document construction sites, work progress, materials, damage, installations or other job-related information. There is no automatic publication or disclosure to unrelated third parties.</p></section>

<section id="s20"><h2>20. Location data and geofencing</h2>
<p>JobStamp may use device location information to provide optional functions such as reminders when arriving at or leaving a customer location, support for time tracking and location-based notices.</p>
<p>Use of location functions is optional and occurs only after explicit consent through the Android permission system. JobStamp does not use location data for permanent movement monitoring or to create movement profiles. Permission can be withdrawn at any time in the system settings.</p></section>

<section id="s21"><h2>21. Notifications</h2>
<p>JobStamp uses local notifications to inform users about important events within the app, such as reminders for time tracking, location reminders, notifications about running work times, synchronisation notices or system messages.</p>
<p>No personal data is transmitted to unrelated third parties for local notifications. Notification permission can be disabled in the device settings at any time.</p></section>

<section id="s22"><h2>22. Audit log</h2>
<p>To improve traceability within a company, certain changes can be logged. This can include, for example, creation or changes to customers and jobs, changes to material data, company settings, team members, as well as additions, changes and cancellations of work-time and workday-timer data.</p>
<p>Depending on the change, the time, type of change, affected record, previous and new value, reason for the change and the user performing the change may be stored. The data is not used for marketing or analytics purposes.</p></section>

<section id="s23"><h2>23. Paid subscriptions (Google Play Billing)</h2>
<p>JobStamp offers optional paid subscriptions that can be purchased through the Google Play Store. Payment processing is handled exclusively by Google.</p>
<p>We do not receive payment information such as credit-card numbers or bank-account details. Only information required for licence management is processed, including product identifier, purchase status, expiry date, technical purchase identifier and licence status.</p>
<p>To prevent misuse, the validity of a subscription may be verified server-side.</p></section>

<section id="s24"><h2>24. Service providers</h2>
<h3>Supabase</h3>
<p>Supabase is used in particular for user sign-in, authentication, database services, cloud synchronisation, storage of company data and permission management.</p>
<p>More information: <a href="https://supabase.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Supabase Privacy</a></p>
<h3>Google Play</h3>
<p>The Android app is distributed through the Google Play Store. When downloading, installing or managing purchases, Google processes personal data under its own responsibility.</p>
<p>More information: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a></p>
<h3>Google Sign-In</h3>
<p>If users sign in with a Google account, authentication is performed via Google's infrastructure. Google's privacy terms also apply.</p></section>

<section id="s25"><h2>25. Data security</h2>
<p>We use appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect personal data against loss, manipulation and unauthorised access. These include, in particular, encrypted data transmission using TLS, secure authentication procedures, role-based access controls, server-side access restrictions and separation of data belonging to different companies.</p>
<p>Despite all security measures, complete security of data transmission over the internet cannot be guaranteed.</p></section>

<section id="s26"><h2>26. Storage period</h2>
<p>Personal data is stored only for as long as necessary for the respective processing purpose or for as long as statutory retention obligations apply.</p>
<p>The storage period depends in particular on the duration of the user account, use of cloud functions, statutory retention obligations and legitimate interests in ensuring the integrity and traceability of company data.</p>
<p>When the relevant purpose no longer applies, personal data is deleted or anonymised unless statutory retention obligations prevent this.</p></section>

<section id="s27"><h2>27. Deletion of user accounts and data</h2>
<p>Users can delete their JobStamp user account directly within the app. The relevant function is available in Settings in the user-account section.</p>
<p>When account deletion is successfully completed, this includes deletion of the JobStamp sign-in account, personal account links, assignments to companies and personal profile data, or—where necessary for business documentation—anonymisation or detachment from the user identifier.</p>
<p>Business data that forms part of a company's documentation is not automatically deleted when an individual user account is deleted. This may include, in particular, jobs, work-time records, material bookings or other company data.</p>
<div class="box important"><p><strong>Special case for company owners:</strong> If a user is the last owner of a company, ownership must first be transferred to another linked user account or the company and its associated company data must be permanently deleted before the user account can be deleted.</p></div>
<p>Account deletion can also be requested without access to the app by emailing <a href="mailto:pabaapps@web.de">pabaapps@web.de</a>.</p>
<p>Further information and full deletion instructions are available on our <a href="/jobstamp/delete-account.html">Delete account &amp; data</a> page.</p>
<p>Where statutory retention obligations or other legal grounds prevent complete deletion, the relevant data will be processed only for the required retention period and deleted afterwards.</p></section>

<section id="s28"><h2>28. Data subject rights</h2>
<p>Under the GDPR, data subjects have in particular the following rights:</p>
<ul><li>Right of access (Art. 15 GDPR)</li><li>Right to rectification (Art. 16 GDPR)</li><li>Right to erasure (Art. 17 GDPR)</li><li>Right to restriction of processing (Art. 18 GDPR)</li><li>Right to data portability (Art. 20 GDPR)</li><li>Right to object (Art. 21 GDPR)</li><li>Right to withdraw consent at any time with effect for the future</li></ul>
<p>To exercise these rights, an informal request to <a href="mailto:pabaapps@web.de">pabaapps@web.de</a> is sufficient.</p></section>

<section id="s29"><h2>29. Right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority</h2>
<p>Data subjects have the right to lodge a complaint with a data-protection supervisory authority if they believe that the processing of their personal data violates data-protection law.</p></section>

<section id="s30"><h2>30. Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>
<p>We reserve the right to amend this Privacy Policy if required due to technical developments, new app functions, changes in legal requirements or other data-protection obligations. The version valid at the time of use applies.</p></section>

